      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T18:24:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Really, this method only needs *either* a `dstCopy` and `dstBounds` OR `dstTextureSampler`, depending on the dst read requirement (`kTextureCopy` versus `kTextureSample`). \nBoth require that the render target be texturable (and check via `Caps::isTexturable`). I\u0027ve made a change that now performs this check not just in the case of a dstcopy but also for the case of dst samples (within `DrawContext`). \n\nThis, combined w/ paints determining dst read strategy by querying Caps, is why we know the dst read strategy will be the same for all draws that require a dst read within a `DrawList` (which informs `RenderPassTask`s).\n\nThough by the time we are beginning a render pass if we know the color attachment is the target, then yes, the texture part can be dropped. Done\n\nThe sampler for a dst copy v. the dst texture should be compatible for both, of course - the lifetime management just differs in the current implementation. I\u0027ve made a change that uses the same sampler creation logic but consolidates it in a way that supports direct or copy dst reads.\n\nTY for the thought provoking comment, this should be more streamlined now!",
      "parentUuid": "38b99ffb_49068063",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 97,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 97,
        "endChar": 45
      },
